From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:13:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Correct TTM windows and the fiscal-year view in the
 calculator

Port of the correctness fixes made on defs/independent-validation, with
no new formula or data:
- TTM sums four contiguous quarters only; a missing quarter is never
  bridged.
- A TTM window that is exactly a fiscal year must agree with that year's
  reported value within the rounding of the five figures, else it is a
  conflict and is not emitted.
- The fiscal-year lookup holds FY flows, year-end balances and
  point-in-time values only, so a Q4 row ending on the same date never
  stands in for the year.
- Market valuations read decimal rows only.
Storage TTM fixtures now carry real quarter starts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CfTpoii6QDStyTPdotmEdY
